==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|festif|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|festivus||pertaining to a feast, gay, lively, joyous|lang=la}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|feast|ive|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-festive.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having the [[atmosphere]], [[decoration]], or [[attitude]] of a [[festival]], [[holiday]], or [[celebration]].
#: ''The room was decked out in '''festive''' streamers, with flowers everywhere.''
# In the mood to [[celebrate]].
#: ''Please put the Christmas decorations away, I'm really not in a '''festive''' mood.''

====Synonyms====
* {{l/en|feastful}}
* {{l/en|feastly}}

